export const _animals_bonobo = {"slug":"bonobo","displayName":"Bonobo","icon":"🦍","description":"Discover perfect bonobo names! 160+ ideas across 8 categories.","metaDescription":"The peaceful primate that resolves conflicts through affection","maleNames":["Ace","Apollo","Archer","Atlas","Axel","Bandit","Baron","Bear","Beau","Bolt","Bruno","Buddy","Buster"],"femaleNames":["Abby","Akira","Angel","Annie","Athena","Aurora","Ava","Bailey","Bella","Belle","Birdie","Blossom","Bonnie"],"cuteNames":["Angel","Baby","Bean","Beau","Biscuit","Blossom","Blue","Bonbon","Boo","Bubbles","Buddy","Bumble","Buttercup"],"funnyNames":["Bark Twain","Chewbacca","Nacho","Pickle Rick","Sir Barksalot","Taco","Waffles","Woofgang Puck"],"fantasyNames":["Aerion","Alduin","Aragorn","Arwen","Aslan","Atreyu","Azrael","Balor","Bastion","Celestia"],"uniqueNames":["Aelious","Bodhi","Caelum","Dune","Elowen","Fjord","Gatsby","Havana","Indigo","Juniper"],"coolNames":["Ace","Axel","Bandit","Blade","Blaze","Bolt","Boss","Bullet","Chaos","Cobra"],"babyNames":["Angel","Baby","Bambino","Bean","Bebe","Bitty","Boo","Bud","Button","Chip"],"faq":[{"q":"Good name?","a":"Match personality, easy to say."},{"q":"By appearance?","a":"Definitely!"},{"q":"Human name?","a":"Very popular."},{"q":"How many?","a":"Pick 3-5, test them."},{"q":"Best sounds?","a":"Vowel endings, esp. 'ee'."}],"seoTitle":"Bonobo Name Generator - Bonobo Name Ideas 🦍","seoDescription":"Find perfect bonobo names! Browse names across 8 categories. Free!","namingGuide":["Observe first.","Easy to pronounce.","Two syllables.","Test a week.","Avoid commands.","Family input."],"habitat":"Bonobos inhabit the dense tropical rainforests of the Congo Basin in the Democratic Republic of Congo, south of the Congo River. They thrive in swamp forests, primary lowland forests, and secondary growth areas. Their habitat is characterized by high humidity, dense canopy cover, and abundant fruit-bearing trees. Unlike chimpanzees, bonobos are restricted to a relatively small geographic range south of the Congo River, separated from chimpanzee populations by this natural barrier.","diet":"Bonobos are primarily frugivorous, with fruits comprising 50-60% of their diet. They also consume leaves, stems, flowers, seeds, bark, and occasionally small mammals, insects, and earthworms. Bonobos are known to share food extensively within their social groups — a behavior less commonly observed in chimpanzees. They forage both in trees and on the ground, spending significant time seeking out ripe fruit across their forest territory.","behavior":"Bonobos are famous for their peaceful, female-dominated social structure and use of sexual behavior to resolve conflicts. Unlike the more aggressive chimpanzee, bonobos resolve tension through social bonding, grooming, and affiliative behaviors. They live in fission-fusion communities of 30-80 individuals, traveling in smaller subgroups during the day. Females form strong coalitions, and male status often depends on their mothers' rank. Bonobos are highly intelligent, using tools in captivity and displaying empathy, cooperation, and complex communication.","facts":"Bonobos and chimpanzees share approximately 98.7% of their DNA with humans, making them our closest living relatives alongside chimps. Bonobos were not recognized as a separate species until 1929. They walk bipedally more often than chimpanzees and have longer legs, a more upright posture, and a smaller head. Bonobos are endangered, with estimates suggesting fewer than 20,000 remain in the wild due to habitat loss and poaching.","naming":"When choosing a name for a bonobo-themed pet or character, consider the peaceful and intelligent nature of these primates. Names meaning 'peace,' 'wisdom,' or 'gentle' fit well. Congo-inspired names honor their geographic origin. Gender-neutral names work well given bonobos' egalitarian society. Consider names like Congo, Rain, Peace, Harmony, Sage, River, Kin, Ember, Zuri (beautiful in Swahili), and Amani (peace in Swahili)."} as const;

